      "writtenOn": "2019-06-14T16:47:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think complicating the build system for this purpose is a too high a price to pay. Also, as most people are not using clang, this compilation mode is prone to getting broken every so often, it just is not viable.\n\nYou are saying it has not bitrotten yet and patches cleanly. Evne if this is merged, when someone makes an incompatible modification clang mode will get broken anyways and you\u0027d have to deal with it.",
      "parentUuid": "f8ec0ffc_95a5da40",
      "revId": "7246553ca669d8a753b536b2b0c118c9691bc996",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8362e427_9830d8a2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1158184
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-14T17:34:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I don\u0027t understand that argument.\n\nYes, if someone makes an incompatible modification in the future, things will break. But it will be easier to fix it then and can quickly be done by anyone rather than the few people who do build with clang on the side and have to carry around out-of-tree patches.\n\nIf there\u0027s basic clang support checked in, it\u0027s also possible to add a test somewhere that builds the EC with clang to catch those breaking modifications automatically.\n\n\"complicating the build system\" mostly involves replacing hardcoded \"gcc\" and \"g++\" strings with $(cc-name) which should be done anyway.\n\nWe\u0027ve had P0s recently where toolchain uprevs broke the tree (e.g. https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EnlFniwIJwU9PkHw486nA2Jca1mbwczl6NnZEPzMZN0/edit?usp\u003dsharing), building with clang regularly might help find those problems earlier.\n\nCost/benefit ratio looks favourable to me :-)",
      "parentUuid": "50be68d9_2c3828e4",
      "revId": "7246553ca669d8a753b536b2b0c118c9691bc996",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "907fbad9_4cc946ac",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-14T17:46:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the change is much more than just replacing gcc with clang, command line options need to be tweaked, conditional compilation sections added, etc.\n\nAnd this will not eliminate the need for thorough testing before upreving the toolchain.\n\nAnd then again, as Patrick points out, we have periodic coverity scan results which greatly go ignored, but could be used to identify fix subtle problems.\n\nMy point is that the prod codebase should not be littered with the one off use case support.",
      "parentUuid": "8362e427_9830d8a2",
      "revId": "7246553ca669d8a753b536b2b0c118c9691bc996",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
