      "writtenOn": "2019-06-12T01:31:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so why does clang warns about it, does it use R7 across this assembler code?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "7246553ca669d8a753b536b2b0c118c9691bc996",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6875a548_37746022",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/build.mk",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-12T16:01:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "clang (and apparently gcc) doesn\u0027t necessarily preserve system registers across inline assembly even if you specify it in the clobber list: https://reviews.llvm.org/D51165\n\nIn this case, we\u0027re not actually clobbering the register in our inline asm. I *think* the original intent was to try to tell the compiler not to modify R7 before entering our inline asm, but dnojiri@ might be the best person to ask since it looks like he wrote it.",
      "parentUuid": "38964ff5_4cf0ae47",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "7246553ca669d8a753b536b2b0c118c9691bc996",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f19fd6e2_7f78b648",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/build.mk",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-12T23:02:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think my intention was to prevent function entry code from clobbering the listed registers. From what I understand now, the clobber list is for showing consistent values to the external code not to the inline assembly.\n\nI kind of remember there is a function attribute to prevent its prologue from clobbering registers (\u0027naked\u0027 or \u0027interrupt\u0027?).\n\nIf we have that, we can get rid of the list, I think.\n\nWhat\u0027s special about R7? It seems it can be saved before inline asm and restored after inline asm like other registers. Maybe it\u0027s used to save \u0026 restore other registers.",
      "parentUuid": "6875a548_37746022",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "7246553ca669d8a753b536b2b0c118c9691bc996",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "273c3afb_cfc05e5e",
        "filename": "core/cortex-m/build.mk",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 39,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-14T00:08:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "RE: R7. It can be used as frame pointer for thumb targets (see section 6.2.5 of http://infocenter.arm.com/help/topic/com.arm.doc.espc0002/ATPCS.pdf) and clang matches gcc\u0027s buggy behavior and doesn\u0027t necessarily preserve the register even when it\u0027s in the clobber list:\n\n\u003e Currently, in line with GCC, when specifying reserved registers like sp or pc on an inline asm() clobber list, we don\u0027t always preserve the original value across the statement. And in general, overwriting reserved registers can have surprising results.\n\n\u003e r7 is used as the frame pointer for thumb targets, and this function needs to restore the SP from the FP because of the variable-length stack allocation a. r7 is clobbered by the inline assembly (and r7 is included in the clobber list), but LLVM does not preserve the value of the frame pointer across the assembly block.\n\nhttps://reviews.llvm.org/D51165\n\nI will double-check the function attribute for preventing register clobbering.",
      "parentUuid": "f19fd6e2_7f78b648",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "7246553ca669d8a753b536b2b0c118c9691bc996",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
